COMPILATION OF: E46L16

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program
S: Symbol Table List

  SYMBOLS:

BLOCK AT LINE 1, AUTO STORAGE 0 BYTES
a 0000 E46L16 ENTRY PARAMETERS(0) EXTERNAL CONSTANT
BLOCK AT LINE 10, AUTO STORAGE 42 BYTES
c 0000 OUTF FILE EXTERNAL STATIC
c 0000 V CHAR(20) VARYING AUTOMATIC
c 0015 W CHAR(20) VARYING AUTOMATIC
   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46L16

   1 a 0000 E46L16:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2a] runtime 5: THREE separate file PUT statements on ONE open stream.  Each is
   4 a 0006      a complete single-item statement, so this is NOT the multi-item shape E46L5 refuses; it
   5 a 0006      is the sequencing question CREATE asks -- does the runtime flush per statement, and does
   6 a 0006      a second PUT start where the first ended?  Expectation: 'AA' + 'B' + 'CC' = 5 bytes, no
   7 a 0006      separator, because the console stream's per-statement line terminator is not reproduced
   8 a 0006      on a stream output file unless the runtime puts one there (unmeasured, so unasserted
   9 a 0006      here and read off DR's own file). */
  10 c 0006   dcl outf file, v char(20) varying, w char(20) varying;
  11 c 0006   v = 'AA';
  12 c 0013   w = 'CC';
  13 c 0020   open file(outf) stream output title('L16OUT DAT');
  14 c 003D   put file(outf) list(v);
  15 c 0055   put file(outf) list('B');
  16 c 006F   put file(outf) list(w);
  17 c 0087   close file(outf);
  18 c 008D   put list('DONE');
  19 c 00A4   stop;
  20 a 00A7 end E46L16;

CODE SIZE = 00A7
DATA AREA = 003D
FREE SYMS = 3838
END  COMPILATION
